 {"id":"fabro-80cc","title":"SENTINEL LOCK PARTNER (do not close): mutual blocker for fabro-919b grill gate","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":4,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:06:01.751Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:52.000Z","description":"Permanent lock partner for fabro-919b. These two sentinels block EACH OTHER (mutual dependency cycle), so both are permanently hidden from 'sd ready' and can never be picked by the develop workflow. sd silently rejects self-dependencies (verified 2026-09-07), which is why the gate needs a partner seed instead. DO NOT close either sentinel, DO NOT remove either dependency edge. Grill-session seeds depend on fabro-919b; when a session concludes, only remove the SESSION seed's edge (sd dep remove <session-seed> fabro-919b) — the sentinel pair stays locked forever and is reusable for future grill sessions.","labels":["grill","needs-user","sentinel"],"blocks":["fabro-919b"],"closedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:52.000Z","closeReason":"retired: lock partner of fabro-919b; ADR-0018 assignee ownership replaces the sentinel mechanism"}
 {"id":"fabro-5e09","title":"Develop planner: pick only seeds assigned to fabro (sd ready --assignee fabro) — deterministic line/user ownership split","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:16:32.837Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:07:20.678Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"GRILL SETTLED 2026-09-07 (user decisions in session):\n\nDECIDED: (D1) The assignee filter for the develop workflow is APPROVED — 'sd ready --assignee fabro' becomes the planner's candidate source. (D2) The REVISOR ASSIGNS NOBODY: filing seeds is its job, ownership is NOT — revisor-filed seeds land UNASSIGNED in the backlog. (D3) Who executes a seed is decided JOINTLY by user + agent (cycle report / grill / chat is the forum; the agent's @fabro assignment is a proposal the user can veto by reassigning anytime). (D4) Fail-closed default (Opt-in): nothing belongs to the line until @fabro is explicitly set. (D5) Emergency channel stays as the standing user directive: when the line/engine is DOWN the agent repairs directly with the user's knowledge (no seed picker involved); the seed is filed retroactively for documentation. No emergency self-service class exists for the revisor or the line.\n\nMECHANISM (line implements, from D1): (1) develop planner prompt candidate source: 'sd ready --assignee fabro --limit 200' (CLI pre-filters — the LLM never sees unassigned/user-owned seeds); (2) goal fast-path honors a named seed id ONLY when assignee is fabro; (3) claim: 'sd update <id> --status in_progress --assignee fabro'; (4) Tracker-empty on the filtered view = legitimate end of work (park) — while the backlog is unassigned the line does NOTHING rather than something; (5) docs/agents/issue-tracker.md documents: assignee is the ownership switch; filers (agent, revisor) file UNASSIGNED; assignment is a joint user+agent decision recorded in the cycle report; (6) revisor seed-intake prompt: remove any language implying the revisor decides execution — it only files.\n\nOWNERSHIP (user decides, NOT the implementer): the existing backlog assignment list is a user+agent joint decision (category proposal from the agent, approval by the user); NO bulk-assign by the develop run. Sentinels (fabro-919b/fabro-80cc) stay until mechanism landed AND backlog curated.\n\nAcceptance: planner prompt ships the filtered command; an unassigned or user-assigned open seed never appears in develop candidates; empty filtered view parks; revisor files unassigned; docs updated; ownership list untouched by the implementer.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-d5fd","title":"Develop planner: probe unfiltered sd list before parking on an empty assignee-filtered view","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:16:29.219Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:26:05.721Z","description":"This run's implementer smoke test showed 'sd ready --assignee nonexistentuser' exits 0 with \"No ready issues.\" — byte-identical to a legitimately empty pool — so under the new park semantics a typo'd or renamed assignee silently parks the line forever. Change: in the FAIL-CLOSED paragraph at .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md:46, before routing Tracker empty, run one unfiltered 'sd list --limit 5' probe; if open seeds exist but the filtered view is empty, journal \"park: N open seeds, none assigned to fabro\" so the terminal Slack notification shows a cause. Effect: converts a silent permanent outage into a visible, diagnosable park; zero added cost in normal runs. Related: fabro-5e09 (the assignee filter this builds on).\nBasis: run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9, workflow version 2232aaf05c7a93b3557b65ef13543486edcf917d0a735f9cb430280339b647a2, commit 6677e200fb8d35e90c2a554bdebe0edc69340394","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-bbbb","title":"Develop planner: drop reasoning_effort from high to low for first-pass claims","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:16:29.325Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:26:05.616Z","description":"In run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9 the planner was the most expensive stage (83.6 s wall = 40% of run, $0.080 = 45% of cost, 4,469 of 5,899 reasoning tokens), mostly tie-breaking two High seeds. The assignee filter this run shipped (fabro-5e09, PR #38) makes 'sd ready --assignee fabro' deterministic, so the tie-break reasoning is wasted. Change: set reasoning_effort=\"low\" on the planner node at .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro:49 (keep high semantics for changes_requested re-plans if conditional effort isn't available; re-measure one run). Effect: ~$0.03-0.05 and 20-40 s off every claim pass.\nBasis: run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9, workflow version 2232aaf05c7a93b3557b65ef13543486edcf917d0a735f9cb430280339b647a2, commit 6677e200fb8d35e90c2a554bdebe0edc69340394","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
+{"id":"fabro-bbbb","title":"Develop planner: drop reasoning_effort from high to low for first-pass claims","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T13:16:29.325Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:38:44.162Z","description":"In run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9 the planner was the most expensive stage (83.6 s wall = 40% of run, $0.080 = 45% of cost, 4,469 of 5,899 reasoning tokens), mostly tie-breaking two High seeds. The assignee filter this run shipped (fabro-5e09, PR #38) makes 'sd ready --assignee fabro' deterministic, so the tie-break reasoning is wasted. Change: set reasoning_effort=\"low\" on the planner node at .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro:49 (keep high semantics for changes_requested re-plans if conditional effort isn't available; re-measure one run). Effect: ~$0.03-0.05 and 20-40 s off every claim pass.\nBasis: run 01M1XZCWNBR33BZGHQXNRA80J9, workflow version 2232aaf05c7a93b3557b65ef13543486edcf917d0a735f9cb430280339b647a2, commit 6677e200fb8d35e90c2a554bdebe0edc69340394","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-513e","title":"Add a just validate-workflows recipe for graph-only validation without a Rust cold build","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:40:03.195Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:43.642Z","description":"In run 01M1XVXF3MJHD0DXVCA7YXDH9G the implementer verified a pure workflow-graph edit by writing a temp integration test lib/components/fabro-validate/tests/tmp_validate_develop.rs and running it: 427,565 ms (~7.1 min cold build), one failure on unresolved_file_ref (@prompts refs), warm re-run 2.9s, then manual deletion — 427s of the 445s implementer tool time (~25% of run wall). Add a just validate-workflows recipe (justfile + small nu wrapper around fabro-validate) that resolves workflow-relative @-refs or scopes out unresolved_file_ref so graph edits verify in seconds. Expected effect: ~7 min and the temp-file dance eliminated on every platform-targeting seed (most of the tracker's High queue); implementer wall drops ~30% on that seed class. Basis: run 01M1XVXF3MJHD0DXVCA7YXDH9G, workflow version 8afe037fc8c61680097f808a27f66ee20da8b546373f6e6e69ad4a09aee94a98, commit 9655d15457db349b4920de1f37eb76338e43eab9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-43ba","title":"Mark no-net-diff churn entries as transient in the develop evidence capture","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:40:09.830Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:43.740Z","description":"The loop-work diff omitted .seeds/issues.jsonl (+1/-1 churn), so the reviewer ran its own git diff <claim-base> -- .seeds/issues.jsonl and found it empty (reviewer journal obs 2); every run churns issues.jsonl on claim/close so this manual fallback fires constantly. Change .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu to annotate churn entries whose net diff vs the claim base is empty with '(transient, no net diff)' or drop them. Expected effect: removes the reviewer's manual git-diff fallback and the risk it escalates to a Verification-blocked cycle. Complements open seed fabro-93a7 (seed-work classification) and is a different mechanism from fabro-1e9f (diff base). Basis: run 01M1XVXF3MJHD0DXVCA7YXDH9G, workflow version 8afe037fc8c61680097f808a27f66ee20da8b546373f6e6e69ad4a09aee94a98, commit 9655d15457db349b4920de1f37eb76338e43eab9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-fb19","title":"Require planner briefs to inline load-bearing engine facts instead of citing source paths","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:40:15.961Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:43.841Z","description":"The planner spent ~4 min verifying engine mechanics (stdin_source resolution, command.output, output.* keys — reading command.rs, context_keys.rs), recorded them as terse path-citing observations, and the implementer re-derived the same mechanics anyway (seq 147-226, minutes of its 15-min inference) — in the stage consuming 86% of run cost (.084 of .256). Change .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 5 (brief-shaping rule): when a brief depends on verified engine mechanics, inline 2-3 exact facts (attribute names + constraints like brace-free stderr, output.<node_id> convention). Expected effect: implementer re-exploration replaced by inlined facts; direct cut into the costliest stage. Basis: run 01M1XVXF3MJHD0DXVCA7YXDH9G, workflow version 8afe037fc8c61680097f808a27f66ee20da8b546373f6e6e69ad4a09aee94a98, commit 9655d15457db349b4920de1f37eb76338e43eab9","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
